      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #60703\n\nWhen a GLM-4.7 model emits a stray <tool_call> in prose\n(e.g. \"I will issue a <tool_call> for it\"), the parser opens\na phantom tool call and silently drops everything that follows:\nthe rest of the content, the real tool call, all lost with\nHTTP 200, finish_reason=stop, no tool_calls, no log warning.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe  state machine was missing a\n transition. When in TOOL_NAME state\nand encountering another TOOL_START, the engine falls through to\n_emit_for_state() which appends the tag text to the phantom\ncall name buffer. The call is then rejected by\n_accept_tool_name() under validate_tool_names=True.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd the missing transition:\n\n\n\nThis closes the phantom call (TOOL_CALL_END) and starts a\nfresh one (TOOL_CALL_START), staying in TOOL_NAME to read\nthe new call name.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Added \n  with 6 regression tests\n- [x] All 6 new tests pass\n- [x] Existing  results unchanged (no regression)\n- [x] Verified before/after: 3 test failures resolved, 0 new failures\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
